Adapted from version 1.3.70, commit 244b957.

Adapted parts. Each file names its source and its changes in its header.

- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/oauth.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/oauth.rs: the authorization URL, the code
  exchange, the token refresh, userinfo, and the rule that refreshes a token
  only when it has less than 300 seconds left.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/client.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/oauth.rs: the client's key name
  (antigravity_enterprise) and the single client it logs in with, read here
  from oauth-client.json.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/oauth_server.rs
  from src-tauri/src/modules/oauth_server.rs: the loopback callback server,
  the state check, the request limits, the 10-minute wait and the pasted
  callback URL.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/token.rs
  from src-tauri/src/models/token.rs: the token record.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/index.rs
  from src-tauri/src/models/account.rs and src-tauri/src/modules/account.rs:
  the account index layout (accounts.json, version 2.0) and the account id.
- crates/quota-station-core/src/antigravity/login.rs
  follows the order of start_oauth_login in src-tauri/src/commands/oauth.rs
  and the invalid_grant handling in src-tauri/src/modules/account.rs.

What was changed:

- macOS only. The Windows and Linux branches, the SQLite store, the
  WebSocket server, wake-up and the other platforms are not included.
- One OAuth client, read from a local oauth-client.json instead of
  constants in the source.
- Tokens are kept in the app's own macOS Keychain items instead of
  AES-encrypted files with their key beside them.
- A thread and blocking HTTP instead of async tasks and Tauri events; typed
  errors that keep no response body, token or secret; no logging.
- The pages the browser sees are translated to Vietnamese, error messages to
  English.

Later milestones that adapt more of Cockpit Tools (reading quota, switching
the Antigravity account) add their parts to this list.
